Pseudoainhum is known to produce a “falsely amputated” appearance of the digit with hyperkeratotic changes reflecting chronic irritation and skin tension. Also, this entity may occur in patients with systemic conditions (such as diabetes) that predispose to such chronic skin changes. Therefore, the most likely diagnosis in this scenario is pseudoainhum.

